# basePath Chapter2

:: FirstContractOpenCh2
@trigger    OnContractSelectOpen
@cutscene
@once

{@Player}   Okay, Mr. Frontier Robotics, got another contract for me?
{@Dorian}   I do. But come on, we're bros. None of this "Mr. Frontier Robotics" stuff.
{@Player}   That's good to hear. I'm not sure everyone else from our old crew feels that way. 
{@Player}	Don't they understand that I need this job so I can pay off the repairs? 
{@Player}	I could lose my ship in a few months.
{@Dorian}   You'll make it. I've got your back. 
    

$call   LockWikiPage("Basic Conductor") // Basic Conductor is replaced with the full version after first chapter 
$call   LockWikiPage("Basic Insulator") // Basic Insulator is replaced with the full version after first chapter 
$call   UnlockWikiPage("Conductor")
$call   UnlockWikiPage("Insulator")

::AfterResearchCh2 

@trigger    OnOverarchingLoaded
@when       IsSolutionFoundFor(Research)
@cutscene 
@once
{@Player}   P.A.L., turns out that material wasn't an insulator. It's a semiconductor.
{@PAL}      Exactly! Great work, Captain.
{@Player}   Exactly? You verified it as an insulator before.
{@PAL}      You're absolutely right. Your research clearly shows that it's a semiconductor.
{@Player}   But you seemed pretty sure before.
{@PAL}      Absolutely! And now we have the correct answer.
{@Player}   ...It's weird how you just keep agreeing with me.

//cut. better to leave the reveal in chapter 9.  The purpose was to expose the fact that PAL is listening to everything. 
//{@PAL}    So Captain, did I overhear that Dorian is your friend? 
//{@Player}   What? How do you- were you eavesdropping? 
//{@PAL}    Oh, yea, I hear every convo you have. 
//{@Player}   ...I see...
//{@Player}   Well, don't feel like you have to listen. 
//{@PAL}    Ah but I have to, in accordance with my Frontier Robotics system parameters. 
//{@PAL}    Even if I wanted to, I can't access the controls to turn it off. 
//{@PAL}    And actually, I enjoy this protocol. It helps me stay on top of things. 
//{@Player}   ...great. 

::BeforeSupplyChainCh2
@trigger    OnOverarchingLoaded
@when       IsSolutionFoundFor(Design), IsSolutionFoundFor(Research)
@cutscene
@once

//introduce the idea of the refining station. pick up at wayward and refine at frosch
{@Player}   Hmmm... looks like I'll need a semiconductor ...
{@Player} I don't see any in this sector.
{@PAL}  You can make one!
{@PAL}     You can get silicon dioxide at Frosch and have the haulers take it to a refinery.
{@Player} A two step process? That sounds pricey.

//cut ?conversation with Taryn and Ovill arguing over who gets to source for Locke. This isn't relevant till level 3 when they can use multiple options.



::AfterSupplyChainCh2
@trigger OnOverarchingLoaded
@when   IsSolutionFoundFor(Design), IsSolutionFoundFor(Research), IsSolutionFoundFor(Supply)
@cutscene 
@once

{@Player}	P.A.L. did you get the fab bay cleaned up? 
{@PAL}		The fab bay is in perfect condition, as always. 
{@PAL}		...at least as perfect as it can be on a near obsolete ship.
{@Player}	Clunker? As always? Looks like someone's system needs some updating...

{@PAL}		[ >_< ]

//call coming in from Quinn
{@Quinn}    Hey Cap'... Frontier Robotics paid your last invoice. What's up with that?
{@Player}   Yeah... I had to take a job with them. Ship repairs put me in some serious debt.
{@Quinn}    Bad luck. I'm not sure about working with those guys...
{@Quinn}    Sure, sure. Just make sure I get paid.
//end call



::AfterFabricationCh2 
@trigger OnOverarchingLoaded
@when   IsSolutionFoundFor(Design), IsSolutionFoundFor(Research), IsSolutionFoundFor(Supply), IsSolutionFoundFor(Fabrication)
@cutscene 
@once

{@Player}   P.A.L.? 
{@PAL}      Yes, Locke? 
{@Player}   What's the deal with Quinn and Frontier Robotics? Is there some kind of bad blood?  
{@PAL}      Frontier Robotics has a stellar reputation! Just check our reviews. We have great cash flow and always pay our invoices.  

